TIME SLOW PROJ

A little project I once started for.. iirc Acerola's game jam.
Didn't finish it back then, but I was bored so I started again.

The reason I'm starting again instead of just continuing is
that the old project was in unity, and.. idk, not feeling
like unity, doing raylib instead.

No idea if this will ever get finished, but rn it's just a
playground for me to program both whatever I want but also
towards a greater goal: A game.

The basic idea of the game is that time changes around you.
Most commonly that'll mean that the further something is from
you, the slower it'll be, but it could also be the other way
around. Might make the gunning gameplay a lil more interesting.
Also lore-wise it's something with science. Otherwise I forgot
almost everything I came up with for the original. Maybe I'll
remember though, once I can see the vision again.

Regarding a license, should I make this open source, I don't
know which one I'll put on this, but know this: I will probably
add some kind of somewhat open license, so if you want to work
on this in private, do that, good chance you'll be able to share
it too. I currently plan on doing it like id-Software does it
with doom: The game's code is open source and free to use, but
the game's data is private so I can still make a profit off of
this. Yall are free to make your own levels though. I bet when
this is done and I show it to my bf, he's gonna make some :3
